   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Trim Burst\n\nShort strokes shoot outward from a point and shrink to nothing: a quick spark, pop or impact accent.\n\nCategory: shapes. Length: 1.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A click, hit, pop or reveal needs a quick burst of lines as a punctuation accent.\n- A UI action or number landing should feel celebratory without a full particle system.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a large, sustained celebration: use confetti or particles.\n- The burst should sit on a moving target: the origin is a fixed point.\n\nVariables:\n- x (number, 0-1): X, default 0.5\n- y (number, 0-1): Y, default 0.5\n- count (number, 1-24): Strokes, default 8\n- inner_radius (number, 0-160): Inner radius, default 16\n- reach (number, 8-240): Reach, default 64\n- stroke_length (number, 4-200): Stroke length, default 56\n- weight (number, 0.5-8): Weight, default 2\n- rotation (number, -180-180): Rotation, default 0\n- spread (number, 15-360): Spread, default 360\n- jitter (number, 0-1): Jitter, default 0.5\n- dots (boolean): Tip dots, default false\n- cap (enum): Cap, default \"round\"\n- color (color): Line color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 1\n- delay (number, 0-30): Delay, default 0\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
